WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.230
- Well, and congrats.

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.059
I mean, you just got a
star on the Walk of Fame.

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:04.892
- [Anthony] Yes I did.

00:00:04.892 --> 00:00:06.197
Yes I did.
- Yes you did.

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:08.080
Was it a weird experience
(applauding)

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.410
where it wasn't just you

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.459
and no one else there?

00:00:10.459 --> 00:00:11.292
(laughing)

00:00:11.292 --> 00:00:12.750
Yeah look, look, it's
just me laying there.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.450
- Look at that beard game, that's you!

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.500
(undecipherable)

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.500
It was, it was me and 11 family
members along with staff.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.400
So yeah, it was just
me and 11 other people.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.233
Yeah, but it was exciting.

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.860
You know I went to the
Hollywood Performing Arts

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.140
Magnet High School, literally
right across the street

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.710
from where I got my star on the corner

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.870
of Hollywood and Highland.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.160
- That's the coolest part.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.010
- Yeah, so never in a thousand years,

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.630
did I think I would be immortalized

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.400
on the Hollywood Walk of
Fame with my own star,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.620
walking those streets every day as a kid.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.950
And even as a young adult,
and to get the call a couple

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.497
of years ago to say,

00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:58.570
"Hey, we'd like to give you this honor."

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:03.410
- Do you still have
moments where you do go,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.920
holy word I shouldn't sound daytime?

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.720
Like it's like I know a
lot of talented singers

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.300
and the fact that I
got to be where I'm at,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.780
I'm always like, sometimes it hits me

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.300
and I'm just like, how
the hell did that happen?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.750
- Yeah, you know my hashtag
on Instagram and Twitter

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.770
is #JustAKidFromCompton you know?

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:19.990
And that's what I am.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.520
I was, I still am just a kid from Compton

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.520
who had a dream and I get to
live that dream every day.

00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:30.740
So yeah, I pinch myself all the time

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.450
and I would be remiss if, can
we get that close right there?

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.420
My buddies George Lopez
and Cedric the Entertainer,

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.720
we all three of us have a star

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:39.860
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.317
And this is our hall of fame--

00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:43.390
- [Kelly] Club?

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.970
- Club, so we each have
a ring with our star

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.190
and the date that we got it.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.790
- It's like your Superbowl ring.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:49.659
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:51.260
- And I wanna thank my boys for that.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.260
- That is so cool.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.312
I wanna be in a club.
(laughing)

00:01:55.312 --> 00:01:57.560
See, I love anything
with everyone's involved

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.240
and there's a jacket or anything involved

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.440
and everyone's wearing it.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.651
You always caption your posts
"Just a kid from Compton"

00:02:03.651 --> 00:02:06.520
Like you were saying, when
did you start dreaming

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.510
to be an actor?

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.351
Were really young?

00:02:08.351 --> 00:02:10.110
- Nine-years-old is--

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.170
- [Kelly] Really?
- when it happened for me.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:14.300
Yeah, and it probably was before then,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.870
but nine-years-old is when
I made the realization

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.930
that this is what I was gonna do

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.882
with the rest of my life.

00:02:19.882 --> 00:02:20.900
- What happened?

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.778
- My mother is a horrible actress.

00:02:23.778 --> 00:02:24.900
(laughing)

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.879
And she was actually in--
- And beats you.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.480
(laughing)
We love your mom right now.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.137
- And she was actually in a production of

00:02:30.137 --> 00:02:33.070
"A Raisin in the Sun" at
Compton Community college.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.650
I'm the oldest of four children and me

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.620
and my two younger
brothers were in the back

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.860
of the theater during rehearsal one day

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.480
and I looked up on stage and
saw my mother rehearsing.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.987
And I said "that is what I'm gonna do

00:02:43.987 --> 00:02:45.150
"with the rest of my life."

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.080
- Oh, that's special.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.759
- It's truly been my calling.
- [Kelly] I think you have

00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:48.810
to dream big on order to get it though.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.730
- Exactly, if you don't, if
your dreams don't scare you

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.323
you're not dreaming big enough.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.740
- Did you ever have, I
was, I grew up with people,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.930
you know, especially a small town

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.670
or just poor community I grew up in,

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.503
everybody would be like,

00:03:02.503 --> 00:03:03.430
"You're never gonna make it doing that."

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.263
- [Anthony] Right.

00:03:04.263 --> 00:03:05.550
- Did you have people
doing that all the time?

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.570
- All the time.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:07.900
- Do you smile so big when you're

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.036
on that red carpet, smiling?

00:03:09.036 --> 00:03:10.310
(laughing)
- [Anthony] I do.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.610
Because I'm not only
smiling for my success

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.720
and for those people
who were the naysayers,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.860
but I'm also smiling for those other kids

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.315
in Compton who were just kids
from Compton who have dreams.

00:03:23.315 --> 00:03:24.660
- Yeah, 'cause you can do it.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.260
- Yeah, exactly.
- I love that.

